{"availability":"available","full":"kydchen/scattered","name":"scattered","description":"A minimalist, local-first canvas for freely arranging and connecting notes—built for Pencil, touch, and mouse.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-28T13:51:39Z","updated":"2026-10-11T03:47:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kydchen.github.io/scattered/","topics":["apple-pencil","freeform-canvas","local-first","mind-mapping","offline-first","pwa","spatial-notes","vanilla-javascript","visual-thinking","whiteboard"],"demo":"https://kydchen.github.io/scattered/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.211Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.211Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.211Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.211Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Scattered is a minimalist, local-first canvas for freely arranging and connecting notes—built for Pencil, touch, and mouse. Write a note, move it anywhere, connect it only when useful, and keep thinking.","There is no account requirement, template, or forced hierarchy. By default, boards stay in the current browser and remain available offline after the app has been loaded once. On the recommended hosted version, connecting Google Drive once on each device can optionally keep the workspace in sync; each Google account has its own isolated workspace. The GitHub Pages version disables Google sync. Both versions stay local unless you explicitly connect Drive or enable a live presentation link."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kydchen/scattered/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cbf582544d26e16e201e09ed564566f9e19ecfa562d30c12c9a32b4ef1091c3b","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.326Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:06.326Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Scattered is a minimalist, local-first canvas for freely arrangi